WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.128
Long ago, Yi Yin was a clever cook.

00:00:04.478 --> 00:00:08.246
He did not only know cooking — he also understood how to govern a country.

00:00:08.596 --> 00:00:12.796
Hearing that Yi Yin was very wise, Tang went in person to visit him.

00:00:13.146 --> 00:00:17.226
The two talked about the great affairs of the world, and found they agreed more and more.

00:00:17.576 --> 00:00:22.184
Yi Yin became a minister and helped Tang govern the country.

00:00:22.534 --> 00:00:26.878
He proposed many good measures, and the people's lives became stable.

00:00:27.228 --> 00:00:32.748
At that time, Jie, the last ruler of Xia, treated the people very badly.

00:00:33.098 --> 00:00:37.178
Yi Yin supported Tang in standing up to oppose Jie of Xia.

00:00:37.528 --> 00:00:42.256
Tang defeated Jie of Xia and founded the new Shang dynasty.

00:00:42.606 --> 00:00:46.422
As the new dynasty began, Yi Yin continued to assist the royal house.

00:00:46.772 --> 00:00:52.028
Later generations looked on Yi Yin as a model of the wise minister.

00:00:52.378 --> 00:00:57.370
However, these stories come from later writings, and the details are hard to verify.

